row(30, 1, 'CONTEXT', f'The receipt-frame that closes the offerings calendar, read with this draft (the draft\'s-grain rule): {HP(30, 1, (("ויאמר", "משה", "אל", "בני", "ישראל"), "and Moses SAID to the children of Israel — the chapter\'s first narrative verb (the store\'s gloss \'and-say\'); the phrase\'s two Bible seats: Bezalel\'s calling (Exodus 35:30) and this; computed"), (("ככל", "אשר", "צוה", "יהוה", "את", "משה"), "according to ALL that the LORD commanded Moses — the receipt formula\'s seven Bible seats: six close ACTS (the tabernacle finished, Exodus 39:32, 42; the census, 1:54; the camp, 2:34; the Levites\' cleansing, 8:20; the Passover, 9:5) and this alone closes a SPEECH — \'and Moses SAID\' (computed on the first word of every seat); the Sifrei 152:1, read whole at sitting 9 and CREDITED here: the frame as punctuation — without it 29:39\'s \'besides your vows\' would run into 30:2\'s vows (R. Yishmael)"))} → {AP(30, 1, (("ואמר", "משה", "לבני", "ישראל"), "and Moses said to the children of Israel"), (("ככל", "די", "פקיד", "יי", "ית", "משה"), "according to all that the LORD commanded Moses"))}. The register: "and he said".')
row(30, 2, 'MATERIAL', f'AND MOSES SPOKE TO THE HEADS OF THE TRIBES — THIS IS THE THING WHICH THE LORD COMMANDED: THE VOWS\' LAW OPENED IN MOSES\' VOICE, NO DIVINE FRAME IN THE CHAPTER; "THE HEADS OF THE TRIBES" THREE BIBLE SEATS. {HP(30, 2, (("וידבר", "משה", "אל", "ראשי", "המטות"), "and Moses SPOKE to THE HEADS OF THE TRIBES — the chapter\'s second and last narrative verb (the store\'s gloss \'and-speak\'); \'the heads of the tribes\' three Bible seats — this and Solomon\'s assembly at the Temple\'s dedication (1 Kings 8:1, 2 Chronicles 5:2); \'TO the heads\' one seat (computed); the Sifrei 153:1: the heads first, then the people — and the release of vows by experts alone"), (("לבני", "ישראל", "לאמר"), "to the children of Israel, saying"), (("זה", "הדבר", "אשר", "צוה", "יהוה"), "THIS IS THE THING WHICH THE LORD COMMANDED — the formula\'s eight Bible seats (the manna\'s two, the tabernacle\'s gifts, Aaron\'s investiture, the eighth day, the slaughter ban, this, the daughters\' marriage at 36:6); the two Numbers seats, chapters 30 and 36, are exactly the book\'s two law chapters WITHOUT \'the LORD spoke to Moses\' — computed on the frames of every chapter; the Sifrei 153:2: \'this is the thing\' — the husband annuls and the sage permits, neither the other; and Moses adds \'this is the thing\' over the prophets\' \'thus said the LORD\'"))} → {AP(30, 2, (("ומליל", "משה", "עם", "רישי", "שבטיא"), "and Moses spoke with the heads of the tribes"), (("לבני", "ישראל", "למימר"), "to the children of Israel, saying"), (("דין", "פתגמא", "די", "פקיד", "יי"), "this is the word that the LORD commanded"))}. The register: "and he spoke".')
row(30, 3, 'MATERIAL', f'A MAN, WHEN HE VOWS A VOW TO THE LORD OR SWEARS AN OATH TO BIND A BOND ON HIS SOUL — HE SHALL NOT PROFANE HIS WORD; ACCORDING TO ALL THAT PROCEEDS FROM HIS MOUTH HE SHALL DO: THE FIRST "WHEN" CASE, TWO DOUBLED ROOTS, THREE ONE-SEAT CLAUSES. {HP(30, 3, (("איש", "כי", "ידר", "נדר", "ליהוה"), "a man, WHEN he vows a vow to the LORD — the first of the chapter\'s two \'when\' cases at the first word; \'he vows a vow\' in this form one seat; the Sifrei 153:3: \'a man\' excludes the minor, and the identity \'vow\'-\'vow\' with the nazirite\'s (6:2) fixes the age — thirteen years and a day"), (("או", "השבע", "שבעה"), "or SWEARS AN OATH — the doubled root; the oath-noun is spelled with the letters of \'seven\' and the parser STARS it as a refused homograph here, at 30:11 and at 30:14 — 3b\'s rule on the seven-stem holding at three new seats (computed)"), (("לאסר", "אסר", "על", "נפשו"), "to BIND A BOND on his soul — the cognate pair\'s one seat; the Sifrei 153:3-4: on HIS soul, not on others\'; bind the permitted, not permit the forbidden; the inward acceptance too"), (("לא", "יחל", "דברו"), "he shall not PROFANE his word — one seat; the profane-verb (the causative of the profane-root) in this sense here alone in the Bible, its five look-alikes \'wait / begin\' in Judges, Isaiah and Psalms (computed); the Sifrei: \'he shall not profane\' and \'you shall not delay\' (Deuteronomy 23:22) — two transgressions on one vow"), (("ככל", "היצא", "מפיו", "יעשה"), "according to all that proceeds from his mouth he shall do — one seat; its two echoes: Moses to Gad and Reuben \'what has gone out of your mouth you shall do\' (32:24, the next portion) and Jephthah\'s daughter \'do to me as went out of your mouth\' (Judges 11:36); R. Akiva\'s equation of the utterance with the oath (153:4); computed"))} → {AP(30, 3, (("גבר", "ארי", "ידר", "נדר", "קדם", "יי"), "a man, when he vows a vow BEFORE the LORD"), (("או", "יקים", "קים"), "or ESTABLISHES AN ESTABLISHMENT — the oath rendered by the stand-root: the translation\'s oath-word is the chapter\'s own confirm-word, cut from the shelf\'s bytes"), (("למסר", "אסר", "על", "נפשיה"), "to bind a bond on his soul"), (("לא", "יבטל", "פתגמיה"), "he shall not VOID his word — \'profane\' rendered \'void\', cut"), (("ככל", "דיפוק", "מפומיה", "יעבד"), "according to all that goes out of his mouth he shall do"))}. No narrative verb — Moses\' speech.')
row(30, 4, 'MATERIAL', f'AND A WOMAN, WHEN SHE VOWS — IN HER FATHER\'S HOUSE, IN HER YOUTH: THE SECOND "WHEN" CASE; "IN HER YOUTH" TWO SEATS, BOTH IN THIS CHAPTER. {HP(30, 4, (("ואשה", "כי", "תדר", "נדר", "ליהוה"), "and a woman, WHEN she vows a vow to the LORD — the second \'when\' case; \'and a woman, when\' three Torah seats: the woman with a discharge (Leviticus 15:19, 15:25) and this; \'she vows a vow\' in this form at Deuteronomy 23:22 (the delay ban), Ecclesiastes 5:3 and here (computed)"), (("ואסרה", "אסר"), "and binds a bond — the Sifrei 153:4: \'a bond\' is an oath, as 30:11 says \'by an oath\'"), (("בבית", "אביה", "בנעריה"), "IN HER FATHER\'S HOUSE, IN HER YOUTH — \'in her youth\' two Bible seats, both here (30:4, 30:17); the priest\'s daughter returns to her father\'s house \'AS in her youth\' (Leviticus 22:13, the kin form); \'in her father\'s house\' one seat, \'her father\'s house\' seven (Tamar\'s widowhood, the priest\'s daughter, this, the slandered bride, Rahab\'s, the concubine\'s two — computed); the Sifrei: her father\'s DOMAIN, and \'a woman... in her youth\' between minority and maturity — twelve years and a day"))} → {AP(30, 4, (("ואתתא", "ארי", "תדר", "נדר", "קדם", "יי"), "and a woman, when she vows a vow before the LORD"), (("ותסר", "איסר"), "and binds a bond"), (("בבית", "אבוהא", "ברביותהא"), "in her father\'s house, in her youth"))}. No narrative verb.')
row(30, 5, 'MATERIAL', f'HER FATHER HEARS AND IS SILENT TO HER — ALL HER VOWS SHALL STAND: THE FATHER\'S SILENCE THE FIRST CONFIRMATION. {HP(30, 5, (("ושמע", "אביה", "את", "נדרה", "ואסרה"), "and her father hears her vow and her bond — the Sifrei 153:5: \'hears\' excludes the deaf; told by others counts too"), (("אשר", "אסרה", "על", "נפשה"), "which she bound on her soul"), (("והחריש", "לה", "אביה"), "and her father IS SILENT TO HER — the silence-verb in this form at two seats, 30:5 and 30:8 (computed); the Sifrei: \'to her\' — he must intend HER; if he thought it was his wife\'s vow he may still annul"), (("וקמו", "כל", "נדריה"), "then all her vows SHALL STAND"), (("וכל", "אסר", "אשר", "אסרה", "על", "נפשה", "יקום"), "and every bond she bound on her soul shall stand — the stand-root twelve tokens in the chapter (computed); the Sifrei 153:5: a vow confirmed for one hour can never be annulled"))} → {AP(30, 5, (("וישמע", "אבוהא", "ית", "נדרה", "ואסרה"), "and her father hears her vow and her bond"), (("וישתוק", "לה", "אבוהא"), "and her father is silent to her"), (("ויקומון", "כל", "נדרהא"), "and all her vows shall stand"))}. No narrative verb.')
