row(30, 9, 'MATERIAL', f'IF ON THE DAY HER HUSBAND HEARS HE RESTRAINS HER AND ANNULS HER VOW WHICH IS UPON HER — THE TWO VERBS TOGETHER: RESTRAINT IS ANNULMENT. {HP(30, 9, (("ואם", "ביום", "שמע", "אישה"), "and if on the day her husband hears — the clock\'s trigger with the construct (one seat)"), (("יניא", "אותה", "והפר", "את", "נדרה"), "he RESTRAINS her and ANNULS her vow — the two verbs side by side: the Sifrei\'s proof that restraint is annulment (153:6, 153:9); the annul-root six tokens in the chapter (computed)"), (("אשר", "עליה"), "which is upon her — the Sifrei 153:10: the vows upon her, not the vows she will make (R. Eliezer\'s a-fortiori refused by the words)"), (("ואת", "מבטא", "שפתיה"), "and the utterance of her lips — the noun\'s second seat"), (("ויהוה", "יסלח", "לה"), "and the LORD will forgive her — the second of the three seats"))} → {AP(30, 9, (("ואם", "ביומא", "דשמע", "בעלה"), "and if on the day that her owner heard"), (("אעדי", "יתה", "ובטל", "ית", "נדרהא"), "he turned her away and VOIDED her vow — \'annul\' rendered \'void\', cut"), (("ומן", "קדם", "יי", "ישתביק", "לה"), "and from before the LORD it shall be forgiven her"))}. No narrative verb.')
row(30, 10, 'MATERIAL', f'THE VOW OF A WIDOW OR A DIVORCED WOMAN — ALL SHE BOUND ON HER SOUL SHALL STAND UPON HER: THE PAIR\'S THREE TORAH SEATS, THE PRIEST\'S DAUGHTER\'S AMONG THEM. {HP(30, 10, (("ונדר", "אלמנה", "וגרושה"), "and the vow of A WIDOW OR A DIVORCED WOMAN — the pair\'s three Torah seats: the high priest\'s forbidden wives (Leviticus 21:14), the priest\'s daughter who returns to her father\'s house (22:13) and this (computed); the Sifrei 154:1: widowed or divorced from MARRIAGE — from betrothal she is still her father\'s (the analogy from the mature daughter who has left his domain); R. Akiva: \'an orphan in her father\'s lifetime\'; the remarried excluded by 30:11"), (("כל", "אשר", "אסרה", "על", "נפשה", "יקום", "עליה"), "all that she bound on her soul shall stand upon her — no one to annul"))} → {AP(30, 10, (("ונדר", "ארמלא", "ומתרכא"), "and the vow of a widow or a divorced woman"), (("יקום", "עלה"), "shall stand upon her"))}. No narrative verb.')
