row(30, 13, 'MATERIAL', f'IF HER HUSBAND ANNULS, ANNULS THEM ON THE DAY HE HEARS — ALL THAT PROCEEDS FROM HER LIPS SHALL NOT STAND; HER HUSBAND HAS ANNULLED THEM AND THE LORD WILL FORGIVE HER: THE DOUBLED ANNUL AT ITS FIRST SEAT, THE LIPS-CLAUSE AND ITS DEUTERONOMY PAIR. {HP(30, 13, (("ואם", "הפר", "יפר", "אתם", "אישה"), "and if her husband ANNULS, ANNULS them — the doubled verb\'s two Bible seats, 30:13 and 30:16, both here (computed); the Sifrei 155:1\'s R. Akiva reads the doubling: annulled in part, annulled in all — against R. Yishmael"), (("ביום", "שמעו"), "on the day of his hearing — the third of the four seats"), (("כל", "מוצא", "שפתיה"), "ALL THAT PROCEEDS FROM HER LIPS — one seat; its pair \'what proceeds from your lips you shall keep\' (Deuteronomy 23:24) one seat (computed); the Sifrei 154:3\'s Hebrew opens on it: the caretaker excluded"), (("לנדריה", "ולאסר", "נפשה", "לא", "יקום"), "for her vows and for the bond of her soul, shall not stand"), (("אישה", "הפרם", "ויהוה", "יסלח", "לה"), "her husband has annulled them, and the LORD will forgive her — the third seat; the Sifrei 154:3: his own act — not her assumption, not the caretaker\'s (R. Yoshiyah); R. Yonatan: the messenger as the man"))} → {AP(30, 13, (("ואם", "בטלא", "יבטל", "יתהון", "בעלה"), "and if her owner VOIDING VOIDS them — the doubling kept"), (("כל", "אפקות", "ספותהא"), "all the outgoing of her lips"), (("בעלה", "בטלנון"), "her owner has voided them"))}. No narrative verb.')
row(30, 14, 'MATERIAL', f'EVERY VOW AND EVERY OATH OF A BOND TO AFFLICT A SOUL — HER HUSBAND SHALL CONFIRM IT OR HER HUSBAND SHALL ANNUL IT: THE AFFLICTION FILTER, THE TWO VERBS ON ONE OBJECT. {HP(30, 14, (("כל", "נדר", "וכל", "שבעת", "אסר"), "every vow and every OATH OF A BOND — the oath-construct starred by the parser (the third refused seat; computed)"), (("לענת", "נפש"), "TO AFFLICT A SOUL — the afflict-infinitive\'s two Bible seats: Pharaoh\'s \'to humble yourself before Me\' (Exodus 10:3) and this (computed; the store\'s gloss \'to-depress\'); the Sifrei 155:1: the husband annuls vows of affliction (this verse) and vows between him and her (30:17) — R. Yoshiyah and R. Yonatan on the vows others could absolve: the fruits of the world, of the province, of this shopkeeper"), (("אישה", "יקימנו", "ואישה", "יפרנו"), "her husband shall CONFIRM IT or her husband shall ANNUL IT — the two verbs with one object: the Sifrei 153:10, \'what came to confirmation comes to annulment\'; 155:1, R. Yishmael (the annulment must cover the whole vow) against R. Akiva (part annulled, all annulled — from these two verbs)"))} → {AP(30, 14, (("כל", "נדר", "וכל", "קיומת", "אסר"), "every vow and every ESTABLISHMENT of a bond"), (("לסגפא", "נפש"), "TO MORTIFY a soul — \'afflict\' rendered \'mortify\', cut"), (("בעלה", "יקימנון", "ובעלה", "יבטלנון"), "her owner shall establish them or her owner shall void them"))}. No narrative verb.')
row(30, 15, 'MATERIAL', f'IF HER HUSBAND IS SILENT, SILENT TO HER FROM DAY TO DAY — HE HAS CONFIRMED THEM, BECAUSE HE WAS SILENT ON THE DAY HE HEARD: THE DEADLINE\'S TWO PHRASES, "FROM DAY TO DAY" AT ITS TWO BIBLE SEATS. {HP(30, 15, (("ואם", "החרש", "יחריש", "לה", "אישה"), "and if her husband is SILENT, SILENT to her — the doubled verb\'s one seat (computed); the Sifrei 156:1: the silence TO VEX (30:12\'s the silence to confirm)"), (("מיום", "אל", "יום"), "FROM DAY TO DAY — two Bible seats: this and 1 Chronicles 16:23, whose Psalm parallel (96:2) writes the same words with the other preposition (computed on both): the Chronicler keeps the Torah\'s form; the deadline — the Sifrei: to the day\'s end, from \'on the day of his hearing\'; R. Shimon ben Yochai: twenty-four hours — the compile\'s clock parameter with two recorded settings"), (("והקים", "את", "כל", "נדריה"), "then he has confirmed all her vows"), (("או", "את", "כל", "אסריה", "אשר", "עליה"), "or all her bonds which are upon her"), (("הקים", "אתם", "כי", "החרש", "לה", "ביום", "שמעו"), "he has confirmed them, BECAUSE he was silent to her on the day of his hearing — the fourth seat of the phrase, and the chapter\'s fourth \'ki\' as \'because\'"))} → {AP(30, 15, (("ואם", "משתק", "ישתוק", "לה", "בעלה"), "and if her owner being silent is silent to her — the doubling kept"), (("מיום", "ליום"), "from day TO day — the Psalm\'s preposition in the translation, cut"), (("קים", "יתהון", "ארי", "שתק", "לה"), "he has established them because he was silent to her"))}. No narrative verb.')
row(30, 16, 'MATERIAL', f'IF HE ANNULS, ANNULS THEM AFTER HIS HEARING — HE SHALL BEAR HER INIQUITY: "AFTER HIS HEARING" ONE SEAT, "HER INIQUITY" THE SUSPECTED WIFE\'S WORD. {HP(30, 16, (("ואם", "הפר", "יפר", "אתם"), "and if he ANNULS, ANNULS them — the doubled verb\'s second seat"), (("אחרי", "שמעו"), "AFTER HIS HEARING — one seat (computed); the Sifrei 156:2: after his CONFIRMATION — the hearing itself is 30:15\'s"), (("ונשא", "את", "עונה"), "then HE SHALL BEAR HER INIQUITY — one seat; \'her iniquity\' five Torah seats: the peace offering eaten on the third day (Leviticus 7:18), the land (18:25), THE SUSPECTED WIFE — \'that woman shall bear her iniquity\' (5:31), the blasphemer (15:31) and this (computed): the husband who annuls after confirming steps into her place; the Sifrei 156:2: the measure of good greater than the measure of punishment — a-fortiori"))} → {AP(30, 16, (("ואם", "בטלא", "יבטל", "יתהון"), "and if voiding he voids them"), (("בתר", "דשמע"), "after he heard"), (("ויקבל", "ית", "חובה"), "then he shall RECEIVE her GUILT — \'bear\' rendered \'receive\', \'iniquity\' rendered by the debt-word, cut"))}. No narrative verb.')
row(30, 17, 'MATERIAL', f'THESE ARE THE STATUTES WHICH THE LORD COMMANDED MOSES — BETWEEN A MAN AND HIS WIFE, BETWEEN A FATHER AND HIS DAUGHTER IN HER YOUTH, HER FATHER\'S HOUSE: THE FOOTER AND THE SIFREI\'S ENGINE. {HP(30, 17, (("אלה", "החקים", "אשר", "צוה", "יהוה", "את", "משה"), "THESE ARE THE STATUTES which the LORD commanded Moses — the footer; \'these are the statutes\' three Bible seats — Leviticus 26:46 and Deuteronomy 12:1 continue \'and the judgments\', this alone bare (computed); the closing \'these\' the architecture measurement\'s footer class"), (("בין", "איש", "לאשתו"), "BETWEEN A MAN AND HIS WIFE — one seat"), (("בין", "אב", "לבתו"), "BETWEEN A FATHER AND HIS DAUGHTER — one seat (computed); the Sifrei\'s engine: \'you are compelled to liken the father to the husband\' — the likening (hekkesh) of this verse decides at four rows where the a-fortiori fails (153:6, 153:7, 155:1, 156:3)"), (("בנעריה", "בית", "אביה"), "in her youth, her father\'s house — the second seat of \'in her youth\'; the Sifrei 156:3: her youth IN HER FATHER\'S HOUSE, not in her husband\'s; R. Yishmael: the betrothed maiden — her father and her husband annul together"))} → {AP(30, 17, (("אלין", "קימיא", "די", "פקיד", "יי", "ית", "משה"), "these are THE STATUTES that the LORD commanded Moses — the statute-word the stand-root: statute, oath and confirmation one Aramaic root in the chapter, cut"), (("בין", "גבר", "לאתתיה", "בין", "אבא", "לברתיה"), "between a man and his wife, between a father and his daughter"), (("ברביותהא", "בית", "אבוהא"), "in her youth, her father\'s house"))}. No narrative verb.')
